<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_TarVault.xml                      UtinniPatches — SUMP_TAR_VAULT_1

  Owner ruling 2026-09-24, typed on the question card, verbatim: "I love
  this, but it requires solvents to extract things or else they are
  rendered useless. So extraction is a solvent based economic need.
  Interesting. Never seen that mechanic before."

  Item spec: "a buildable tar-pit store (pit or sunk barrel-rack). Anything
  sealed in it is perfectly preserved — food, corpses, hides never rot.
  Sealing is cheap; the tar does the work... retrieving an item without
  solvent yields it tarred/ruined (useless). Cleaning it out costs solvent
  per item — the same acid as SUMP_GASLIGHT_1's reaction (one acid, three
  uses)... rot-stop is a container comp (vanilla-adjacent); the gate is an
  extraction bill/job consuming solvent, else the tarred variant comes out."

  Base chosen: ParentName="StorageShelfBase" (Data/Core/Defs/Core/
  ThingDefs_Buildings/Buildings_Furniture.xml, read in full this pass via
  RimSage) — a real, already-proven vanilla storage-furniture chain
  (thingClass Building_Storage, ITab_Storage, StorageSettings) rather than a
  hand-rolled container. "Sealing is cheap" needs no bespoke seal action at
  all: ordinary vanilla hauling AI already carries a matching item into any
  Building_Storage's cells the moment its filter allows it — the comp below
  starts sealing the instant that happens.

  Comp: RimMandrake.TheSump.CompProperties_TarVaultSeal (this item's own new
  C#, mandrake.rm.thesump — see that file's header for why it lives in
  TheSump's own assembly rather than the shared mandrake.rm.
  environmentalhazards one this Sump kit otherwise concentrates generic
  mechanisms in: EnvironmentalHazards is a sibling FOUNDRY pass's contended
  file today, and this mechanism is Sump-specific — a single building type,
  not a cross-biome primitive like RM_TarCoatingUtility). CompRottable.
  disabled (a real public field, confirmed via RimSage against RimWorld/
  CompRottable.cs) is vanilla's own "this thing does not rot right now"
  switch — no RotProgress bookkeeping needed. Extraction is a Gizmo command
  (CompGetGizmosExtra), NOT a WorkGiver/JobDriver pair: a full haul-to-
  container job pair needs live verification this pass had no bridge access
  for (no unattended guessing at a RimWorld API per CLAUDE.md), and an
  administrative Gizmo interaction is itself a real, provable mechanism
  (the same "immediate command, not a walked job" shape CompRefuelable's own
  manual reload commands and Building_Storage's own per-item select gizmos
  already use in vanilla).

  Storage filter: default narrowed to Foods/Corpses/Leathers (the item's own
  "food/corpses/hides"), replacing StorageShelfBase's broader default list —
  a full <categories> redeclare, which RimWorld's XML inheritance treats as
  a full replace of that one list field, same as Shelf's own
  relatedBuildCommands redeclare demonstrates for a different list on the
  same base chain. fixedStorageSettings (the hard cap, which excludes large
  corpses via specialFiltersToDisallow) is left INHERITED, unmodified — a
  known, flagged limitation (a giant creature's corpse cannot be vaulted)
  rather than a guess at loosening a filter this pass could not live-test.

  storageGroupTag repointed to its own tag so vaults link/rename as their
  own group, distinct from ordinary Shelf furniture.

  Research: RUT_TarRendering — SUMP_GASLIGHT_1's own build note flagged this
  ResearchProjectDef as "defined but deliberately left UNWIRED to anything
  ... a future pass wiring the discovery comp decides what 'first meeting
  tar' should gate, if anything beyond flavor." This pass wires it for real,
  as ordinary manually-completable research (not the discovery-trigger
  mechanism, which stays INDIGENOUS_TECH_REVISIT_1's own gated scope) — "the
  Sump's tar gives up more than it takes, once someone works out how to
  handle it... waterproofing, adhesive, road-metal, fuel" is a genuine
  thematic fit for "how to seal things in it so they keep."

  Cost: Bitumen (the tar's own reward material, SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1 §4)
  alongside stuff-costed structure, on the same "the tar does the work"
  logic RUT_GaslightLamp.xml already costs its Sumpgas-burning fixture in
  Bitumen too.

  Texture: gen_tarvault_placeholder.py, same flat-fill-plus-outline posture
  every sibling placeholder in this pass uses — checked infrastructure/
  artpipe/done, _artsrc and registry.jsonl for "tarvault"/"tar vault"/
  "larder" first (0 hits) per CLAUDE.md's "check for existing regenerated
  art before queuing more". Real (hand-authored, reviewed) art is owed.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="StorageShelfBase" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.thesump">
    <defName>RUT_TarVault</defName>
    <label>tar vault</label>
    <description>A sunk barrel-rack packed in black Sump tar. Anything lowered into it stops aging the moment the tar closes over it — food stays fresh, a corpse stays whole, a hide stays supple, for as long as it sits sealed. The tar does not let go easily: pulling something back out clean takes a solvent to cut the seal, or it comes up ruined, fused uselessly into the tar that kept it.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/RUT_TarVault/RUT_TarVault</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(2,1)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <size>(2,1)</size>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <costStuffCount>16</costStuffCount>
    <costList>
      <RUT_Bitumen>10</RUT_Bitumen>
    </costList>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>120</MaxHitPoints>
      <Mass>10</Mass>
      <WorkToBuild>800</WorkToBuild>
      <Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <building>
      <storageGroupTag>RUT_TarVault</storageGroupTag>
      <defaultStorageSettings>
        <priority>Important</priority>
        <filter>
          <categories>
            <li>Foods</li>
            <li>Corpses</li>
            <li>Leathers</li>
          </categories>
        </filter>
      </defaultStorageSettings>
    </building>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Styleable" />
      <li Class="RimMandrake.TheSump.CompProperties_TarVaultSeal">
        <scanIntervalTicks>60</scanIntervalTicks>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>RUT_TarRendering</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
    <designationCategory>Furniture</designationCategory>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
